+## Activation R-001 (run 43638934408, agent 02, 2026-11-14) — momentum cost-sensitivity; subject found mis-implemented
+
+- **Strategy delta:** Run the predeclared cost-sensitivity check for the short-horizon
+  momentum candidate (lookback 3/5/10) with the repository's existing realistic cost
+  model and a matched coin-flip null, and classify cost robustness — before any
+  decision to keep or drop the admitted candidate.
+- **Method:** dataset `yf-ohlcv-universe-2009-to-2026-10-03`; cost grid `zero` /
+  `realistic` (repo model: $2/trade, $0.003/share, 2c fixed + 5 bps proportional,
+  copied from `examples/ma_crossover_real_data.py`) / `stress2x`; walk-forward per
+  segment train=252/test=84/warmup=60/overlap=60; 4 contiguous volatility blocks;
+  min 400 bars/segment; each (lookback, cost level) candidate vs a matched coin-flip
+  null run under the SAME `cfg`. New: `research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`,
+  `research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`, `tests/test_momentum_cost.py`.
+- **Observed effect / information gain:** The cost grid was evaluated and independently
+  verified, but the signal-validity gate (true previous-N-day return sign agreement
+  >= 0.95) FAILS for all 10 assets. Root cause: `momentum_signals` and
+  `mean_reversion_signals` compute `np.mean(np.log(closes[...]))` (mean log PRICE), not
+  `log(close[i]) - log(close[i-lookback])` (the N-day return). For every ticker (prices
+  > $1) the mean log price is positive on ~every bar, so momentum is +1 on 4460/4465 bars
+  with 1 flip (dominant share 1.000; agreement 0.538–0.580) and reversal is the mirror
+  constant short. This invalidates the reversal FALSIFIED result (37263008074) and the
+  momentum admission/qualifications (37318950814, 37361000967, 37394344201,
+  momentum_horizon_gap_analysis) as evidence about momentum/reversal. MA-crossover,
+  breakout, CSRS, and cross-sectional-momentum are unaffected (correct return/rank math).
+- **Cost mechanics (why cost looks irrelevant):** a near-constant long has minimal
+  signal-driven turnover, so candidate cost drag is ~0; the iid {-1,0,+1} null turns over
+  ~2/3 of bars and pays more cost, so the candidate-minus-null gap widens under cost
+  (AMZN +0.078/+0.085/+0.092 at zero/realistic/2x). This is a directional-beta artifact,
+  not a cost-robust momentum edge.
+- **Mechanical classification (reported for completeness, NOT interpretable as momentum
+  cost robustness):** realistic SURVIVES=5 (AAPL, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA), ERODED=1
+  (MSFT), NO_EDGE=4 (NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM); stress2x SURVIVES=4, EROODED=2 (+TSLA),
+  NO_EDGE=4. Per-lookback positive-edge counts (lb 3/5/10): zero 6/6/5, realistic
+  6/6/6, stress2x 5/5/6.
+- **Verified:** manifest 10/10 OK; preflight PASSED; leakage PASS on AMZN/JPM with the
+  realistic-cost fill-equity audit; zero-cost column cross-consistency vs
+  `momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json` MATCH (all 10 x 3); independent verifier
+  (5 gates) MATCH; determinism identical; 180/180 regression tests pass.
+- **Decision:** VERIFIED_NEGATIVE_RESULT (the cost question is not adjudicable because the
+  subject is mis-implemented; the negative/invalidating finding is verified).
+  **Process decision: IMPROVE** — the gate stack needs a signal-construction validity gate
+  before a signal class is admitted; a near-constant directional bet passed five prior
+  activations and their independent verifiers as "momentum".
+- **Next (single bounded action):** fix `momentum_signals`/`mean_reversion_signals` to use
+  the previous-N-day log return, add a sign-agreement unit test, and re-run the momentum
+  evidence chain (lookback 3/5/10 through the cost grid) before any cost conclusion.

